   "gap": "Vaught 1961 Sec. 5 (pp. 315-318) is not presented anywhere on the route: Theorem 5.2 (prime model and aleph_0-universal homogeneous model under the hypothesis of 5.1, via Ehrenfeucht's cited 5.1, 3.5, 4.8), Theorem 5.3 with its proof (a prime model of an aleph_1-categorical, non-aleph_0-categorical T has no proper elementary submodel, by the omega_1-chain of prime models), and Theorem 5.4 with its proof (in an aleph_1-categorical T every definable set is finite or of the model's power, via Theorem 4.2 applied to two relative interpretations in T'). These are prime/countable-model results with proofs in the complete 1961 contribution 303-321; Secs. 1-4 and the p. 315 examples are complete in the n-a-003-01 presentation and Sec. 6 is in n-a-004-01.",
